  "description": "BUJZOZ crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C65 H123 Cr2 Dy4 F2 N3 O26. From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 7 O neighbors; Dy4 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Cr1 (Cr) has 5 O neighbors; Cr2 (Cr) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 7 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.315-4.105 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 95.17-108.82°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C65H123Cr2Dy4F2N3O26.",
